---
import '../styles/global.css';
interface Props { title: string; description?: string; }
const { title, description } = Astro.props;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const current = Astro.url.pathname;
const navLinks = [
  { href: `${base}/#read`, label: 'read' },
  { href: `${base}/mixing-lab/`, label: 'mixing lab' },
  { href: `${base}/structure-lab/`, label: 'structure lab' },
];
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#f3f4f1" />
  <link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 viewBox=%220 0 100 100%22><circle cx=%2238%22 cy=%2242%22 r=%2230%22 fill=%22%237b5cf0%22/><circle cx=%2262%22 cy=%2258%22 r=%2230%22 fill=%22%23ffe600%22 style=%22mix-blend-mode:multiply%22/></svg>" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bodoni+Moda:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..96,400..700;1,6..96,400..700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;1,400&display=swap" />
  <title>{title} | Why Glass Has Color</title>
  {description && <meta name="description" content={description} />}
</head>
<body>
  <nav class="site-nav wrap" aria-label="Site">
    <a class="brand" href={`${base}/`}>Why glass has color</a>
    {navLinks.map((l) => (
      <a href={l.href} aria-current={current === l.href ? 'page' : undefined}>{l.label}</a>
    ))}
  </nav>
  <slot />
  <footer class="site-footer wrap">
    <div><p><b>How the colors are made.</b> Absorption curves are illustrative, drawn from the shape of published spectra rather than measured. Each is converted to optical density, scaled by amount and thickness (Beer–Lambert), multiplied against the lamp's spectrum (CIE D65 daylight unless you change it), integrated with the CIE 1931 2° observer on a 5 nm grid, adapted toward D65 as far as the eye adapts to that lamp (fully in daylight, partly under candle, tungsten, LED and tube, not at all under a sodium lamp) and encoded as sRGB.</p></div>
    <div><p>Source and data on <a href="https://github.com/Jacob234/glass-color-explainer">GitHub</a>.</p></div>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
